# Add-lift catalog search

Search Exercises in the add-lift dialog must **visibly filter the catalog as the user types**. It is not a stub, not a global shortcut, and not a freeform prescription parser.

Source of truth: `knowledge.md` Add lift (RTS-style: category, search, exercise, then variation chips). Do not implement `design.md` §6.2 two-pane builder or §7.3 mobile bottom-sheet / Create Custom from query.

## Diagnosis (do not re-litigate)

Wiring already exists and **does filter in memory**:

- `AddLiftBar` holds `search` and `options = filterCatalog(category, search)` (`src/components/AddLiftBar.tsx`).
- Input `data-testid="add-lift-search"` updates `search` (`placeholder="Search"` — the **S** the user pointed at).
- `filterCatalog` substring-matches `item.name` only (`src/services/exerciseCatalog.ts`). Unit test: `search finds bench across categories`.

It **feels dead** because matches are only `<option>`s inside a **closed native `<select data-testid="add-lift-exercise">`**. Typing never reveals a list, count, or empty state. User Defined hides the select and ignores search. Stale `exerciseName` can remain selected after it drops out of `options`.

The **S** is the Search placeholder, **not** a keyboard shortcut. Do not add ⌘S, `/`, or an S keycap.

## Product verdict

| Keep | Drop |
| :--- | :--- |
| In-memory `CATALOG_EXERCISES` + `filterCatalog` as the only filter | Backend / remote exercise search |
| Category **AND** search (constraint × query) | Replacing category with search-only |
| Explicit **User Defined → Misc** custom name field | Auto-creating a lift from the query string |
| Then `LiftVariationPicker` chips | Starting-set editor in this dialog |
| Structured pick from catalog | Parsing prescriptions / aliases from freeform text as the lift |
| Catalog bundled in the client (works offline) | Network fetch, debounce for ~25 rows |
| Visible results list (RTS picker) | “Just shrink the closed `<select>` options” |

Naive “filter the `<select>`” is **insufficient**. Smallest change that makes search real: **show the filtered catalog in the dialog**.

## Spec

### Query (`filterCatalog` only — do not duplicate in the component)

- Trim; case-insensitive.
- Split on whitespace; **every token must match** (AND).
- A token matches if it is a substring of any of: `name`, `movementPattern`, `category`, `liftCategory`, or a compact **alias** list on that row (or a small `EXERCISE_ALIASES` map). Examples: `bench` → Bench / Close Grip Bench / Incline Bench; `hip` → Hip Dominant rows; `rdl` / `romanian` → RDL if aliased; `close bench` → Close Grip Bench.
- Empty query + empty category → **full catalog** (scrollable list, not an empty “Select exercise”).
- Empty query + category → that category only.
- `category === 'User Defined'` → `[]` (search does not apply).
- Rank: name prefix, then name includes, then pattern/category/alias. No fuzzy/Levenshtein.
- **No debounce.** Catalog is tiny and local.

### Category × search

- Both apply (AND). Knee Dominant + `press` → Leg Press, not Bench.
- Changing category still clears the selected exercise (existing). **Keep** the search string.
- Do not auto-set category from a search hit until the user **picks** a row (`pickExercise` may still fill category when it was empty).

### User Defined

- Catalog list hidden; custom name field stays.
- Disable or ignore Search; helper: `Catalog search does not apply. Name this lift.`
- Custom lifts still store `movementPattern: 'Misc'`.
- No-results must **not** auto-switch to User Defined. User picks that category.

### UI (AddLiftBar)

- Keep the centered dialog, Category select, Search input, then variation chips. No nested cards, no two-pane split, no Comp/Variation/Accessory tabs.
- **Replace the closed native exercise `<select>`** with a visible listbox (`role="listbox"`) of catalog rows. Max-height + `overflow-y: auto`. Each row: exercise **name** (optionally muted pattern). Click = existing `pickExercise`.
- Autofocus Search when the dialog opens.
- Empty query: list is the filtered catalog (all or category).
- No matches: `data-testid="add-lift-no-results"` copy **No catalog matches.** Hint: clear search, change category, or pick User Defined to name a custom lift.
- If the selected exercise is not in `options`, **clear selection** (Confirm must not stay enabled on a hidden pick).
- Clear-search control when query is non-empty (optional `[x]`). Do not hijack Escape — `CenteredDialog` already closes on Escape.
- Keyboard in the list: ArrowUp/ArrowDown highlight; Enter picks highlighted (from search field, Enter picks first/highlighted match if any).
- Placeholder may stay `Search` or become `Name, pattern, or category`. No S-shortcut badge.
- `LiftVariationPicker` only after a pick. Confirm still requires `selected`.

### Offline / RBAC / locks

- Catalog-only; no new API. Works offline.
- No extra RBAC; add-lift already uses session write.
- Do not add search on locked/finished sessions beyond existing Add lift visibility.

### Tests

- Extend `src/services/exerciseCatalog.test.ts`: name; pattern (`vertical`); category token (`hip`); AND with category constraint; User Defined → `[]`; aliases if added; multi-token AND; empty query returns catalog (not empty).
- E2E: type in `add-lift-search` and **assert visible names without `selectOption`**. Cover: `bench` shows Bench variants; click + Confirm adds the lift; `zzzz` shows no-results; Knee Dominant + `press` is Leg Press not Bench; User Defined hides results.
- Update `e2e/session.spec.ts` and `e2e/reorder.spec.ts` — they use `add-lift-exercise` `selectOption`. After listbox, pick by test id / role option (e.g. `add-lift-result-Squat` or `getByRole('option', { name: 'Squat' })`).
- Keep `data-testid="add-lift-search"`. Add `add-lift-results` on the listbox. Prefer `add-lift-result-{name}` per row.

